okay I need to talk to you about  something really important today and I  need some time to lay this all out for  you but hopefully it'll be productive  yesterday I started getting emails and  seeing comments saying David will you  disclose your funding and will you  disclose whether you're getting money  from a pro Bashar al-asad group that is  in existence to prop up the Syrian  regime disclose your funding and tell us  who your funders are and it seemed like  a weird thing to ask of me I didn't  understand why are people coming to me  and saying am i getting funding from a  from a probe Bashar al-asad group so I  started researching this and then I saw  a couple of reports and posts that there  are several left-wing independent media  people that have allegedly received  money from a pro-assad group some under  the guise of a journalism award money  that was awarded for winning a  journalism prize so I want to do this  and I'm gonna give you the full  breakdown of our revenue at the end of  the segment but let's go through this  and actually try to do it right so let's  begin with what are the allegations the  allegations are that several left-wing  independent media hosts and writers and  publications received money from a group  called the Association for investment in  popular action committees it's a very  sort of innocuous name but investigative  reporting by Charles David claims to  demonstrate that this is actually an  umbrella organization that is covering  for and the sort of a name placeholder  for a groups that are Pro Syrian  dictator Bashar al-assad the Association  for investment in popular action  committees has a trademark called the  serious solidarity movement which again  it sounds Pro rights but it's its  pro-assad and the idea here is that this  is an umbrella group for pro Syrian  government organizations when you look  at them on guidestar it's very innocuous  it's a civil rights advocacy group  organized in 2007 there's limited  information it's headed up by two guys  Paul LaRue Dee and Kamal obeyed and when  I started looking into this and this is  all new to me I've you know I did did  the research over the last 24 hours  obaid has said that he  a member of architects and engineers for  9/11 truth which is a 9/11 truther group  I would call it a conspiracy group so  it's starting to get a little bit weird  and the revelations that have come  forward for independent media are that  this group has created something called  the Serena shim Award for uncompromised  integrity and journalism which Awards  money to different media people they've  paid former Ohio Democratic governor  Dennis Kucinich $20,000 to speak at a  pro Bashar al-asad conference in the  United Kingdom and it so happened that  Kucinich opted not to condemn Assad a  few years ago and it turns out that some  people including former TYT host jimmy  dore door a I don't know how the name is  pronounced now as well as youtuber Kim  Iverson who I didn't know much about and  many others have received money from  this group through this award now let's  go through it there are some trends that  exist here both door and Iverson have  done a combination of questioning the  known facts about Bashar al-assad and  have started to dabble in some  conspiratorial false-flag stuff as well  both door and Iverson have put out  content that is very Pro tulsi gabbard  and Tulsi has her own sort of history  with Assad that has been a subject of  scrutiny there is an IRS filing which  you can easily find online from the  pro-assad group which shows that in 2017  door received twenty five hundred  dollars from this group while Kim  Iverson previously posted to Instagram  that she received five thousand dollars  from the group so the first question is  can we trust the allegation in other  words did these people and the others  that are listed in the piece that we're  linking to did they receive this money  Iverson admits she got the money she  posted about it and unless the IRS  filings are false door did as well  there's a longer list of people you can  find online but did part one did they  get the money it appears that they did  so then we have to ask well even if it's  a pro-assad group that is funding the  award are they is is are they getting  money to say certain thing  or are they merely being awarded for the  things that they're already choosing to  say and I think that this is an  important distinction with a lot we've  talked about this before you know that  it's common that people at Fox News  people at RT Russian television they'll  say nobody ever comes in and tells me  exactly what I need to say and of course  it doesn't work that way it's not say  this stuff and then we will pay you it  is often that people are selected for  roles on the basis of what they're  already likely to say so we really don't  know the reality of this that's one  thing then there's this issue you know  it it correlates with the pro tulsi  stuff and alternative facts around Syria  and related topics this is odd but  ultimately it's their business now if it  were me I would disclose this stuff  full-stop I mean I don't I don't have  any other way that I would qualify it I  would just disclose it so then we come  to me and the emails I've been getting  over the last 14 16 hours saying David  you're part of this disclose your  funding we want to know where you get  your money so I'm gonna do that first of  all I don't know why anyone would think  I'm getting money from a pro-assad group  or pro-assad sources particularly ones  that are peddling and you know we're  their leaders the disobeyed guy pedals  in 9/11 truth or stuff or anything I  don't do any of what they do you know I  I don't do Assad apologetics I don't do  Pro tulsi apologetics I don't do any of  this stuff but I'll just come clean and  tell you our funding this is from a  normal month this is data from August  the but we it's the beginning of October  so I haven't closed the books on  September yet but this is a typical  month this is August we got 40% of our  revenue from memberships patreon and  apparel 32 and a half percent from  YouTube ads 22% from ad sales three and  a half percent from twitch as many of  you know we're new to twitch so that's a  pretty small part of our revenue right  now Facebook ads we're now monetizing on  Facebook but only about 1% of our  revenue and miscellaneous donations are  0.1% now those miscellaneous donations  of course could come from anybody but  what I'm talking about is sometimes  people don't want a membership they'll  just send us you know a check for a  little bit of money and that was 0.1% of  our funding back in August we don't take  money from any groups if we have an  advertiser it  Martha's an advertisement if we do a  sponsored video its marked as a  sponsored video that's it so I can't  speak to the strategy behind other  people's actions I have no idea what  people's financial situations are and  what would cause them to accept or not  accept money from an organization like  this everybody's financial situations  are different and also I don't know if  what people are concerned about is that  the the content of these programs is  influenced by the fact that they've  received money from this group or if  people are concerned about the lack of  disclosure or something else and it  would be interesting to clarify that but  to be very clear  people are often chosen for awards  because they're saying the right things  and of course the award can be a way to  funnel money to someone under the guise  of we are rewarding you for good  reporting or whatever the case may be  but typically that's not how it works  people people are brought in or  supported because they're already saying  the things that the funder wants them to  say so that's our funding I can't speak  for anybody else and I hope that this  will sort of put to bed the questions  I've been getting over the last half day  or so

